---
args: { input: CaseInput }
returns: RunProposal
---
1. Bind `goal = await frameRequest(input)` from the request and `policy = await selectPolicy(input)` from supplied authority candidates. Preserve unresolved precedence instead of guessing which source governs.
2. Bind `work = await formTaskGraph(goal)` and `evidencePlan = await planEvidence(input, work)` so each operation has explicit prerequisites and a searched source universe.
3. Run the stages in their dependency order. The first stage receives only `input.domainRecords.firstStage`; every later stage receives the preceding function's actual accepted records. Bind each full result separately.
const defineUseContractResult = await defineUseContract(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan);
const writeAnnotationSpecResult = await writeAnnotationSpec(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, defineUseContractResult.accepted);
const auditCandidatesResult = await auditCandidates(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, writeAnnotationSpecResult.accepted);
const measureCoverageResult = await measureCoverage(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, auditCandidatesResult.accepted);
const commissionAndReleaseResult = await commissionAndRelease(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, measureCoverageResult.accepted);
4. Bind `stageSet: CaseStageSet = { defineUseContract: defineUseContractResult, writeAnnotationSpec: writeAnnotationSpecResult, auditCandidates: auditCandidatesResult, measureCoverage: measureCoverageResult, commissionAndRelease: commissionAndReleaseResult }` and `collection: CollectionFinding = await reconcileCollection(stageSet)`. Bind `allQuestions: string[] = [...defineUseContractResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...writeAnnotationSpecResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...auditCandidatesResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...measureCoverageResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...commissionAndReleaseResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...collection.coverageGaps]` and `questions: QuestionBatch = await resolveQuestions(allQuestions, input)`.
5. Bind `invalidation = await assessDelta(input)`, `review = await prepareReview(collection)`, and `view = await composeView(review, input)`; pass each child its actual declared inputs and retain the returned object.
6. Bind `allChecks: CheckResult[] = [...defineUseContractResult.checks, ...writeAnnotationSpecResult.checks, ...auditCandidatesResult.checks, ...measureCoverageResult.checks, ...commissionAndReleaseResult.checks]`. Bind `hasGateFailure = allChecks.some(check => check.verdict !== "pass")` and `hasBlocker = input.authorityStatus !== "authorized" || questions.questions.length > 0 || collection.coverageGaps.length > 0`. Bind `disposition: "proposed" | "blocked" | "needs-review" = hasBlocker ? "blocked" : hasGateFailure ? "needs-review" : "proposed"`. Bind `rationale: string[] = allChecks.map(check => `${check.check}: ${check.verdict}; evidence ${check.evidenceIds.join(",")}`)`.
7. Operational detail 1 — A source license permits research but not redistribution: enforce the release boundary. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (enforce the release boundary.) through the existing stage result for DatasetUse; preserve exact source/version and the prior DatasetUse, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
8. Operational detail 2 — Near-duplicate records cross train and test: group by underlying source before splitting. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (group by underlying source before splitting.) through the existing stage result for DatasetUse; preserve exact source/version and the prior DatasetUse, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
9. Operational detail 3 — A label requires information not present: revise the task or mark it unobservable. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (revise the task or mark it unobservable.) through the existing stage result for DatasetUse; preserve exact source/version and the prior DatasetUse, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
10. Operational detail 4 — A coverage target is met through copied examples: count independent mechanisms and sources. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (count independent mechanisms and sources.) through the existing stage result for DatasetUse; preserve exact source/version and the prior DatasetUse, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
11. Operational detail 5 — Consent is withdrawn after release: maintain traceable removal and downstream notification obligations. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (maintain traceable removal and downstream notification obligations.) through the existing stage result for DatasetUse; preserve exact source/version and the prior DatasetUse, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
12. Initialize `revisions: RevisionProposal[] = []`. If any gate is not pass, bind `revision = await proposeRevision(the failed check names, the smallest affected stage name)` and add that returned proposal to revisions. Bind and return `result: RunProposal = { caseId: input.caseId, goal, policy, work, evidencePlan, defineUseContract: defineUseContractResult, writeAnnotationSpec: writeAnnotationSpecResult, auditCandidates: auditCandidatesResult, measureCoverage: measureCoverageResult, commissionAndRelease: commissionAndReleaseResult, collection, questions, invalidation, review, view, revisions, disposition, rationale }`. Proposed actions remain proposals. The host owns authorization, persistence, effect dispatch and verification.
